  "rationale": "There are at least two independent ways to reach crownData:exfiltrate. (1) iotDevice:exploitPublicApp (from wifiGuest or internet) leads to configSecret:credentialAccess, then fileServer:lateralMovement, then dbReplica:collection, then crownData. (2) browserStore:credentialAccess (from workstation:exploitPublicApp or dmzWeb:execution) leads to jumpHost:lateralMovement, then shareMount, vaultRead or mailArchive, then crownData. No step lies on both paths, so blocking any single step leaves the target reachable. Even dbReplica:collection is not critical, because jumpHost still reaches crownData through shareMount, vaultRead or mailArchive."
